# Next / React / Tailwind

## App Router

- Pages stay thin: load data/compose, put interaction in `src/components/`
- Mark interactive trees with `"use client"` at the leaf that needs state/effects — not the whole app by default
- Fonts via `next/font` CSS variables (`--font-sans`, `--font-display`); wire in `layout.tsx`
- Import UI with `@/components/...`, never deep relative hops from `app/`

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
export default function Home() { /* big stateful planner here */ }

// ✅ GOOD
export default function Home() {
  return <PlannerApp />;
}
```

## React

- Functional components + hooks only
- Hydrate localStorage behind a `hydrated` flag so SSR and first paint match
- Prefer controlled local state; no new global store unless asked
- Typed props interfaces; export named components (`export function X`)

## Tailwind v4

- Utility classes in JSX; shared tokens in `globals.css` (`:root`, `@theme inline`)
- Use existing palette (`background`, `foreground`, teal/amber accents) — don’t invent a second theme
- Responsive with `sm:` / grid utilities already used in pickers
- No new CSS frameworks or UI kits

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<div style={{ color: '#2dd4bf' }} />

// ✅ GOOD
<div className="text-teal-300/70" />
```
